<div
  class="table-scroll"
  tabindex="0"
  role="region"
  aria-label="Array operation complexity"
>
  <table>
    <caption>Dense textbook dynamic array · n values · index i</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Operation</th>
        <th scope="col">Time</th>
        <th scope="col">Why / auxiliary space</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Read / update by index</th>
        <td>O(1)</td>
        <td>Address calculation; O(1) space.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Traverse all values</th>
        <td>Θ(n)</td>
        <td>Visit every value; O(1) space without collecting output.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Unsorted linear search</th>
        <td>O(1) best; O(n) worst; Θ(n) average*</td>
        <td>Stop at a match, or scan all values; O(1) space.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Append with doubling</th>
        <td>O(1) amortized; O(n) worst</td>
        <td>
          Resize occasionally copies n values; O(n) temporary space during
          growth.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Insert at i</th>
        <td>O(1 + n − i) without growth; O(n) worst</td>
        <td>
          Shift suffix right; O(1) space without growth, O(n) if resizing.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Remove at i</th>
        <td>O(n − i); O(n) worst</td>
        <td>Shift suffix left; O(1) space. No shrinking in this model.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="complexity-note">
  *Average search assumes a successful target equally likely at each position.
  Missing targets require n comparisons. Unit-cost fixed-width values,
  arithmetic and comparisons are assumed. Backing storage uses O(capacity)
  space; after many removals, retained capacity may greatly exceed length.
</p>
